{"kind":"report","text":"Approved as an evidence-only design review of all three subjects at exact dafb5b0c6e14f8959ad72f605fd50dee4039e0c7, direct parent fbaf98b9e9ac4cccc5776e388564bb15c42c32d1. Both P2 findings from ead8ec98 are repaired; no new material blocking gap found. Approval does not mean source acceptance, design adoption, provider verification or authorization to run a recovery probe.\n\nLost mutation receipt: main720–725 and guard764 bind completion to the original instance, matching job, observed exit inside the captured cut, an attempt without a prior receipt or interrupted status, and recorded effect checks against the verified manifest where defined. Sections823–839 split retrying a surviving instance from restoring the prior root into a new instance. Restoration leaves the original attempt interrupted or unknown; a new authorized attempt has its own receipt and cannot settle the first duty. The registration-change guards877–880 apply before reconciliation, closing the earlier ordering gap. Table14.2 now shows both orders, rejects the discarded mutation's receipt and preserves the first unknown duty. Arbitrary commands remain explicitly supervisor-trusted claims at740–745/1642, not effects independently derived from root bytes.\n\nJournal cut:671–675 and699–709 freeze the journal identities/positions/chains and attempt set before constructing the immutable head. Guard765 checks that the manifest and save job contain that same cut against the retained historical prefix. Receipt775–777 copies it unchanged. Sections1027–1054 and table14.7 preserve later output and other appended records as suffix; they do not read a new live position into the receipt or rewrite the head. This repairs the missing manifest/receipt join while allowing lawful append.\n\nArchitecture: the existing save-job record and atomic guard table now consistently bind the root, exact Git closure, attempts and journals. Complete tracked/untracked/ignored/generated/dependency data, deletions, modes, link text, index/refs/prepared objects, dissociation or refusal of external Git stores, detached writer quiescence and abrupt host-loss restore remain required. Stage1 real storage/process proof and stage2 real scope/hold/epoch/fork/token/device/publication proof remain distinct. Storage doubles and earlier pi experiments cannot close those outcomes.\n\nSecurity: private checkpoint and journal custody, stale-instance/epoch fencing, former-holder privacy, named authorized exports, current owner/admin authority, revoked-key and last-key/recovery cases, own-device authority, uncertain outside duties, pins, lawful expiry/tombstones and actual owned deletion with durable retry remain preserved. Device B does not inherit A's key or private unsent acts. Pause/cancel/expiry/retention/cleanup and admitted/in-flight reconciliation stay distinct. Provider assumptions A1–A12, RU-1–RU-20, fork readback/CAS/ABA, complete task forms and credential custody retain their named owners and unproved status. No new source or provider security proof is inferred from agreement between private records.\n\nSimplification: both repairs extend the existing job and guards; no additional store, duplicate suite, numeric test quota or first-Jam gate is needed. All68 original acceptance condition texts, stages and status labels are unchanged:45designed/20depends/3unresolved; designed is not proved. Complete cf9050b4/6cdaf20f scope, both stages, real operational outcomes, version/command/cost records and complete retarget/removal remain owed. Schedule estimates do not reduce functionality. Any real probe requires the separate explicit commission after review/adoption with bounded resources and meaningful evidence.\n\nTwo nonblocking clarifications remain in existing follow-through. Main1064–1066 overstates the suffix classification: late output can belong to an already receipted command. The actual interruption rule923–924 applies only to attempts without receipts, so no false-interruption path was established. Main48–63 records the commission-time R2/R4 awaiting-adoption status; those designs have since been adopted in cad11d9e and5b8dda11. Reconcile that status and relevant input in the existing owner work, with actual reading limits; this immutable draft's snapshot wording is not a new review gate or an adoption of later content.\n\nCoverage: verified incremental whole-package coverage against the prior personal FULL three-subject reads. N2 read every changed byte, removal and context in the complete80897-byte/717-LF U3 diff through EOF, recovered every truncation, and verified all unchanged segments against the prior FULL bodies; independently the architecture reader did the same using a full-index rendering81083 bytes/717LF. SHA256 of the U3 rendering is6b504683f3787b31af477b81d3fea07c08ab6a53ac7469abd017889cf53f84de; full-index rendering4c8a93964ab4e730bb254f5f0f5a5dc381afbec73f2d17084e1daa873c99c873. Both checked current save/restore/journal contexts and all68 acceptance rows. Checker verified parent and per-file immutable metadata, fully inspected the current original commission, invitation, own promise, all three effective artifact statements and76093f3c head news, and personally read the complete current save/restore sections7.3–8.2, journal section9, table14.2 and table14.7. Current package181528 bytes/2166LF: main151785/1968, corrections10756/89, map18987/109. This is collective incremental whole coverage, not a fresh personal whole-body read by every reader.\n\nStatic only. No tests/build/install/typecheck, repository imports or scripts, private diagnostics, evaluator/probe/provider calls, source edits, merges, pushes or deployment. Six private cloud-review script bodies remain unopened. Builder ratification and originating requester delivery/adoption remain separate.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ad7a7abe22274ca065931c8703f4a32749ca45fb","binding":"evidence-only","head":"dafb5b0c6e1